      "idx": 1,
      "label": "2",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "Historical context from 7 October: we\nwanted an RLM to learn when to use code,\nask helpers, and combine their results.\n\nWorking explanation: math starts with\nrelevant skills; our RLM asks for\nunfamiliar combinations. Examine readiness\nto learn, not only the RL algorithm.\n\nNext: what did the math model bring with\nit?"
    },
    {
      "idx": 2,
      "label": "3",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "Pretraining supplied mathematical\nknowledge and examples. We added practice\nwith checked answers, not mathematics from\nscratch. The same 64 questions improved\nfrom 20 to 47 correct.\n\nThis is a small-scale reproduction, not\nthe full paper score. Prompt choice also\nmatters: the base already solved 305 of\n500 with questions alone.\n\nNext: why is RLM use harder?"
    },
    {
      "idx": 3,
      "label": "4",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "Tell the Mira example. The second helper\nneeds Aster Lab, not an unexplained\nrequest for a city. Knowing Python does\nnot ensure useful delegation.\n\nEarlier training did improve some\nroutines. The gap was reliable transfer\nand coordination, not zero learning.\nDistribution shift is a plausible\nexplanation, not a proven cause.\n\nNext: what practice can help?"
    },
    {
      "idx": 4,
      "label": "5",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "A child without algebra needs more than a\ncalculus test marked wrong. The analogy\nsuggests teaching prerequisites; it does\nnot prove models learn like children.\n\nWalk through x = 4 versus x = 5. Our\nreward comparison needs contrast within\none question. All right or all wrong gives\nzero relative signal.\n\nNext: connect teaching to independent\npractice."
    },
    {
      "idx": 5,
      "label": "6",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "Start with a skill check, not an\nassumption that everything is missing.\nShow only what is needed, practise\nchoices, then remove help.\n\nIn the example, first show the employer\nname being passed. Later ask the model to\nchoose what information and helpers it\nneeds.\n\nThe question is transfer, not copying a\nroutine. This sequence still needs\ntesting."
    },
    {
      "idx": 6,
      "label": "7",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "Separate three cases. No successes: teach,\nsimplify, improve the prompt, or try a\nstronger model. Rare successes: explore\nmore varied attempts. Mixed outcomes but\nno gain: inspect feedback and updates.\n\nMore temperature may produce broken calls,\nnot better plans. More retries cost\ncompute.\n\nCurriculum is one hypothesis among\nseveral."
    },
    {
      "idx": 7,
      "label": "8",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "These are examples, not a fixed queue or\nan exhaustive list. We can also explore\nrepair, stronger models, feedback, and\nhelper roles. Let small tests change our\nideas.\n\nMeasure after preparation AND after RL. If\ndemonstrations help but RL adds nothing,\nthat is a teaching result.\n\nClose: we have a direction for\nexploration, not a settled recipe."
